      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x-8{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x-8{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -\\frac{7x}{8x(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int -\\frac{7}{8(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{8}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{8}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
